---
title: Proposed player-owned memory and gameplay
---
sequenceDiagram
  accTitle: Proposed player-owned gameplay connects durable evidence and semantic skills without granting memory execution authority
  accDescr: A scoped memory packet informs one player. The player requests a semantic skill, which executes bounded primitives through the current controller and native gate. Observations and unknown effects are retained for state and work revision. At the end or an unexpected outcome the player assesses and replans. User Pause blocks further dispatch. Optional curators propose lessons, while reusable library changes have separate tests and review. Participants are logical responsibilities, not required separate processes or models.
  participant M as Evidence and<br/>campaign views
  participant P as One player
  participant S as Skill executor
  participant G as Current gate
  participant C as Windowed CDDA
  M->>P: Bounded state / work / source packet
  P->>S: Semantic goal and stop conditions
  loop Bounded skill with fresh checks per primitive
    S->>G: Proposed primitive
    G->>C: Input only with current authority
    C-->>G: Visible result
    G-->>M: Retain evidence / unknown disposition
    G-->>S: Actual result for progress or stop
  end
  S-->>P: Completion / partial / unknown and evidence
  P->>M: Revise scoped understanding and pending work
  Note over G,C: User Pause blocks further dispatch,<br/>committed effects cannot be undone
  Note over M,P: Optional curator proposes lessons,<br/>reusable library changes need separate tests/review
